desc: Loop the Loop Looper (mda Looplex port) by chmaha
tags: looper loop delay overdub midi
author: chmaha
version: 1.0
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  Looping delay for live looping, with up to 200 seconds of memory. Press Record (or the sustain pedal,
  CC64) to start: the first pass sets the loop length, pressing again stops recording and the loop plays on;
  record again to overdub. Feedback sets how much of the loop survives each pass, and the mod wheel (CC1)
  turns it down further. CC66 or CC67 (sostenuto or soft pedal) jumps back to the start of the loop. As in
  the original, the loop is stored at 16-bit resolution with dither. Max Del sets the memory size: it applies
  at once while the looper is empty, and never wipes a loop (a new size waits for Clear Loop, which stops
  recording and erases the loop). MIDI passes through; the loop is not saved with the project, but Export
  Loop puts it on a new track as an audio item.
  Ported from mda Looplex by Paul Kellett (Maxim Digital Audio), via mda-effects
  https://github.com/pluginguru/mda-effects (MIT or GPLv2+)
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
